CFO Decision Dashboard Case Study
Project Summary
This project presents a CFO decision dashboard designed to help finance teams analyze budget vs. actual spend, monthly burn rate, department expenditure, and expense category variance.

Business Objective
The objective was to create an executive-level view that makes it easier to monitor spending, identify overspending, and support better financial decisions.

Problem Statement
Finance leaders often need to answer quickly:

Are we within budget?

Which departments are spending the most?

Which categories are driving cost?

How is spending changing over time?

This dashboard was built to make those answers visible in one place.

Key Metrics
Total Budget

Total Actual Spend

Variance Value

Variance Percentage

Monthly Burn Cash

Department Spending

Expense Category Distribution

Insights From the Dashboard
Actual spend exceeded budget, which suggests a need for tighter cost control.

Department-level spending makes it easier to identify high-cost functions.

Expense category analysis highlights where costs are concentrated.

Monthly burn trends provide visibility into how spending changes across the year.

Value to the Business
This dashboard supports decision-making by turning raw finance data into a clear executive view. It can help leadership track budget performance, detect overspending, and improve financial planning.

Skills Demonstrated
KPI design

Financial reporting

Data visualization

Executive storytelling

Dashboard layout and design

Conclusion
This project shows the ability to build a finance-focused dashboard that communicates business performance clearly and supports better decision-making.
